; Regression: the pointee exemption is about NULLABILITY, not about being a
; pointee (2026-08-28).
;
; null_set_target# lets `set r: null` through when the POINTEE of a `ref[T]`
; may itself hold nothing. A scalar pointee may not, so a `ref[int]` out-cell
; keeps the first gate's verdict: storing null through into a non-optional
; pointee is the same lie one level in, and the 193 scalar out-cells converted
; on 2026-08-27 must stay judged.
;
; xfail: null assigned to a non-optional reference

procedure zero(out: ref[int])
    set out: null

var n 7
zero(&n)
Console.println "`n`"
